dsh-math — internal development and review package

This package includes local Math Harness P2-C runtime files under runtime/p2c.
It also includes new fixed checkers whose exact Ring15, Q7 and grid75 algorithms
were derived from harness/dsh-p3a/image/math/checker.py, and new M-pilot files
using design patterns from the local preflight and P2-C adapter. Original paths,
current hashes and reference hashes are recorded in PROVENANCE.json. No legacy
six-task executor, live entry, authorization data, credentials or model catalog
is bundled.

No explicit license grant covering these local prototype files was found.
This notice does not grant redistribution rights or relicense those files.
The package is private and marked UNLICENSED. Public redistribution requires
confirmation from the relevant rights holders, including the project's local
prototype contributors. No copyright owner is inferred from a filesystem path.

Runtime peers (not bundled): DeepSeek Harness / Cordis packages (MIT), React
(MIT). dsh-codex (Apache-2.0) is an optional separately installed companion;
its code and credentials are not bundled. The original notices of any peers
remain in their separately installed packages. Python and Node runtimes are
also external requirements and are not included in this archive.

Research contracts contain byte-preserved copies of the three local candidate
problem cards. Research materials, papers, attachments, run logs and exports
are user data with separate rights and are not otherwise included in the plugin
installation archive. Scientific review and execution authorization remain
separate from this package notice.
